From 72ac9d8630bf63ae7ffd43212163299071e1a29e Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: ayiejosh <132535860+ayiejosh@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sat, 10 Oct 2026 19:41:38 +0800
Subject: [PATCH 070/294] pco: unroll loops of at most 128 iterations

max_unroll_iterations also scales NIR's unroll size budget (26 times the
iteration limit). With 1024, CTS synchronization tests that copy a
64x64x8 image in a single invocation had two nested 64-iteration loops
unrolled into ~41k instructions, and pco_trans_nir_vec(), whose search
for each source's parent is a backward linear scan, then spent over 15
minutes in pipeline creation (98 cases of
dEQP-VK.synchronization.op.*.(read|write)_image_*.image_64x64x8_r32_sfloat).

With 128 those cases compile in ~0.5 s and pass. Every benchmark shader
(vkrender, vkheavy, cstp/cstpf/cstpi, vkmany, internal shaders included)
compiles to the same binary.

CTS (synchronization list 1718 + 5062 + 9170 + 838 + 282 cases) was run
with this and the other three commits of this series applied: identical
to before, except one case that ran into the kernel's 500 ms job timeout
(memory.pipeline_barrier.graphics.host_write_vertex_buffer.1048576_vertex_buffer_stride_2,
which passes in 20+ other runs; kernel timeout recovery bug). weston +
weston-simple-egl + vkcube: OK.
---
 src/imagination/pco/pco_nir.c | 2 +-
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/src/imagination/pco/pco_nir.c b/src/imagination/pco/pco_nir.c
index afe65935..1f3043b0 100644
--- a/src/imagination/pco/pco_nir.c
+++ b/src/imagination/pco/pco_nir.c
@@ -82,7 +82,7 @@ static const nir_shader_compiler_options nir_options = {
 
    .lower_helper_invocation = true,
 
-   .max_unroll_iterations = 1024,
+   .max_unroll_iterations = 128,
    .max_samples = 4,
 
    .io_options = nir_io_vectorizer_ignores_types,
